-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",64,{
[2017]="700169E8\n1\tThe refugees are outside of the library, near the craft-hall, watching the Rangers train, and by the stable-master in Esteldín. Halbarad is not convinced of Narmeleth's intentions, but has allowed you to question the Hillman-refugees from Angmar.\t\n2\tTalk to Halbarad at Esteldín\tHalbarad is in Esteldín in the North Downs. You should return to Halbarad and inform him that one of the refugees is missing.\n",
[2018]="700169E9\n1\tFind the missing refugee\tThe missing refugee might be found in the eastern-most pass between the North Downs and Angmar. Halbarad instructed you to search for signs of the missing refugee.\n2\tTalk to Halbarad at Esteldín\tHalbarad is in Esteldín in the North Downs. You should return to Halbarad and inform him that the refugee was a spy.\n",
[2019]="700169EA\n1\tTalk to Narmeleth at Delossad\tNarmeleth is at Delossad in Tâl Bruinen. Halbarad has asked that you bring his thanks to Narmeleth for her aid in saving Esteldín.\n",
[2020]="700169EB\n1\tHear Narmeleth's tale and experience 'Session: Daughter of Strife' or read the shortened account instead\tNarmeleth is being held prisoner in Delossad in southern Trollshaws. You should speak with Narmeleth and hear the tale of her downfall. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tTalk to Narmeleth at Delossad\tDelossad is in the Trollshaws, south-west of Rivendell. There Narmaleth wishes to speak with you.\n",
[2021]="700168FC\n1\tAccompany Glorfindel to the final Council\tGlorfindel is in Rivendell, south-east of the House of Elrond. Narmeleth has asked you to speak with Glorfindel on her behalf.\n2\tTalk to Glorfindel\tGlorfindel is in Rivendell by the Falls of Imladris, south-east of the House of Elrond. You should return and speak with Glorfindel in Rivendell.\n",
[2022]="700169DD\n1\tTalk to Narmeleth at Delossad\tDelossad is in the southern Trollshaws, south-west of Rivendell. Narmeleth has asked to speak with you at once.\n",
[2023]="700168FB\n1\tTalk to Golodir at Gath Forthnír\tGath Forthnír is in the north of Angmar, north-east of Imlad Balchorth. Narmeleth is ready to travel to Gath Forthnír and speak with Golodir.\n",
[2024]="70000683\n1\tBring the sigils back to Radagast the Brown at Ost Guruth\030Collect sigils from gaunt-men (total: 5)\tThe gaunt-men dwell in the ruins to the far east of Haragmar. Radagast told you of the gaunt-men, necromancers in the service of Sauron, who are responsible for the emergence of these wights. He asked you to defeat the war-singers and bring him their sigils. He can then determine which of the Gaunt-lords they serve.\n",
[2025]="70000684\n1\tTalk to Aric the Stone-speaker in Harloeg\tAric is south of Ost Guruth, beyond Talath Gaun, down in Harloeg. Radagast spoke of a Man named Aric the Stone-speaker. Aric may be able to tell you the history of the Red Swamp.\n",
[2026]="70000694\n1\tTalk to Emelin\tEmelin haunts the area called Ost Haer. Aric spoke of a shade called Emelin. If you can prove your worth to the shade, he might give you the information you desire.\n2\tTalk to Emelin at Ost Haer\tEmelin haunts the area called Ost Haer. Emelin has tasked you with defeating the apparitions of his dead warriors. Succeed, and he will help you. Fail, and you may perish.\n",
[2027]="70000699\n1\tDefeat Brudhraw\tThe wights and their wight-lord may be found west of Ost Haer in Nindor. Emelin told you that the Gaunt-lord Ivar the Blood-hand raises the wights as his soldiers. You must destroy them and their lord, a wight called Brudhraw.\n2\tTalk to Emelin at Ost Haer\tEmelin is at Ost Haer, to the north. You defeated the wight-lord Brudhraw. Now you should return to the shade called Emelin.\n",
[2028]="70000685\n1\tTalk to Radagast the Brown at Ost Guruth\tRadagast the Brown is in the tower at the end of the main avenue in Ost Guruth. Emelin told you his sad tale, then instructed you to return to Radagast the Brown.\n",
[2029]="7001C685\n1\tTalk to Radagast the Brown at Ost Guruth\tRadagast the Brown is in the tower at the end of the main avenue in Ost Guruth. Radagast the Brown waits to lead you into the passage to Agamaur. When you are prepared to leave, you should speak with Radagast again.\n2\tTalk to Elsa in Agamaur\tElsa is in the camp within the ruins. You should speak with Elsa about your victory within Agamaur.\n3\tTalk to Radagast the Brown in Agamaur\tThe Eglain and the shades of Arthedain have established a small encampment within the ruins. Elsa of the Eglain waits to speak with you. Your battle against Ivar's darkwater was a victory, or so it appears. The Gaunt-lord retreated into the north, pursued by Radagast the Brown, and has not been seen since.\n",
[2030]="70000686\n1\tTalk to Radagast the Brown at Ost Guruth\tRadagast the Brown is in the tower at the end of the main avenue in Ost Guruth. Radagast the Brown waits to lead you into the passage to Agamaur. When you are prepared to leave, you should speak with Radagast again.\n2\tTalk to Elsa in Agamaur\tElsa is in the camp within the ruins. You should speak with Elsa about your victory within Agamaur.\n3\tTalk to Radagast the Brown in Agamaur\tThe Eglain and the shades of Arthedain have established a small encampment within the ruins. Elsa of the Eglain waits to speak with you. Your battle against Ivar's darkwater was a victory, or so it appears. The Gaunt-lord retreated into the north, pursued by Radagast the Brown, and has not been seen since.\n",
[2031]="7000069A\n1\tSpeak with Elsa the Bold\tElsa is in the Agamaur camp. Radagast thanked you for your help and asked you to speak with the Eglain woman named Elsa.\n2\tBring Elsa's pack to Hana\tThe passage to Haragmar lies to the south. Ost Guruth is west of Haragmar. Elsa gave you a letter to deliver to Frideric requesting supplies for her encampment. She also asked you to deliver a pack to her sister, Hana. Both can be found in Ost Guruth.\n3\tBring Elsa's letter to Frideric the Elder\tFrideric abides in the courtyard of Ost Guruth. Hana was pleased to receive the pack from Elsa, knowing that her sister is watching out for both her and all of the Eglain.\n",
[2032]="70013AF3\n1\tDefeat gredbyg within the Great Delving (total: 12)\tGredbyg can be found throughout the Great Delving, to the south and west of the Chamber of the Cross-roads. Bósi has asked you to eliminate the fierce gredbyg within the Great Delving. These insects are a threat to the safety of the dwarves.\n2\tTalk to Bósi\tBósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, at the southern entrance to Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving. You have defeated many of the gredbyg in the Great Delving, helping to make the area more safe for Bósi's dwarves.\n",
[2033]="70000707\n1\tDefeat melee White Hand Orcs (total: 8)\030Defeat ranged White Hand Orcs (total: 6)\tWhite Hand Orcs infest the Weather Hills, west of Candaith's camp. The Ranger Candaith offered you assistance in finding Radagast the Brown in exchange for aid against the Orcs in the Weather Hills.\n2\tTalk to Candaith at his camp\tCandaith is at his camp near the foot of Weathertop, among the Weather Hills. While you were fighting the Orcs, Candaith began his search for Radagast the Brown.\n",
[2034]="70061BF1\n1\tDefeat Orcs in the ruins of Tharbad (total: 8)\tOrcs prowl the ruins of Tharbad and should be opposed by whatever hearty folk encounter them.\n2\tTalk to Meneldir by the northern bank of the Gwathló\tMeneldir and Egfrith are resting by the northern bank of the Gwathló.\n3\tTalk to Egfrith by the northern bank of the Gwathló\tMeneldir and Egfrith are resting by the northern bank of the Gwathló.\n4\tScout camp-fires to the west of the broken bridge in Tharbad\tEgfrith suggested you deal with Orcs at the camp-fires to the west, on the other side of the broken bridge, enabling the three of you to plan your travel through the Orc-occupied city and beyond.\n5\tHelp the man engaged in combat with the Orcs to the west\tA man fights with Orcs to the west of the broken bridge in Tharbad. He could need your help!\n6\tTalk to the Orc-slaying stranger in Tharbad\tThe travelling clothes in which the man is dressed cannot hide the fact that he is a proven warrior. The bodies of the Orcs about his feet also do much to make that clear.\n",
[2035]="70041322\n1\tTalk to Captain Maeral of the Alphroval, the northernmost ship docked at the wharf\tMaeral is the captain of the Alphroval, the northernmost of the ships docked at the wharf at Dol Amroth. Lothíriel has asked you to visit the captains at the wharf, in order to assess the sea-worthiness and battle-readiness of their ships.\n2\tLook at the Sea-gate from the deck of the Alphroval\tThe deck of the Alphroval, northernmost of the ships docked at the wharf in Dol Amroth, will give you a good vantage from which to look at the Sea-gate. Captain Maeral wants you to look at the Sea-gate from where you stand on the deck of his ship.\n3\tTalk to Captain Maeral of the Alphroval, the northernmost ship docked at the wharf\tMaeral is the captain of the Alphroval, the northernmost of the ships docked at the wharf at Dol Amroth. You have done as Captain Maeral asked, and should now speak with him about what you saw.\n4\tTalk to Captain Noreth of the Rosigil, the easternmost ship docked at the wharf\tNoreth is the captain of the Rosigil, the easternmost of the ships docked at the wharf at Dol Amroth. Lothíriel has asked you to visit the captains at the wharf, in order to assess the sea-worthiness and battle-readiness of their ships.\n5\tNoreth wants you to stand on the deck of her ship and look through the Sea-gate\tThe deck of the Rosigil, easternmost of the ships docked at the wharf in Dol Amroth, will give you a good vantage from which to look through the Sea-gate, there to see whatever it is that Captain Noreth wants you to see. Captain Noreth wants you to look through the Sea-gate from where you stand on the deck of her ship.\n6\tTalk to Captain Noreth of the Rosigil, the easternmost ship docked at the wharf\tNoreth is the captain of the Rosigil, the easternmost of the ships docked at the wharf at Dol Amroth. You have done as Captain Noreth asked, and should now speak with her about what you saw.\n7\tTalk to Captain Cirnaith of the Súlrohir, the southernmost ship docked at the wharf\tCirnaith is the captain of the Súlrohir, the southernmost of the ships docked at the wharf at Dol Amroth. Lothíriel has asked you to visit the captains at the wharf, in order to assess the sea-worthiness and battle-readiness of their ships.\n",
[2036]="70000705\n1\tBring the Orc-orders to Candaith\030Collect the Orc-orders\tThe Orc-messenger is surely at one of the enemy camps in Glumhallow, west of Candaith's own encampment at the foot of Weathertop. An Orc-messenger made his way from the Midgewater Pass to the outlying Orc-camps located throughout the Weather Hills. Candaith asked you to intercept the Orc-messenger and return with the orders he must bear.\n",
[2037]="70061BF2\n1\tRecover Boromir's pack from the Orc-thief somewhere to the south-west\tThe Orc-thief that ran off with Boromir's pack is likely somewhere to the south-west of his position in Tharbad.\n2\tReturn the stolen pack to Boromir to the north-east\tBoromir is to the north-east, in Tharbad, taking stock of the situation and planning his next steps.\n3\tCollect scattered supplies to the west of Boromir's position in Tharbad (total: 3)\tIn his haste to escape, the Orc-thief tried to empty the stolen pack of some of its contents, which are now scattered to the west of Boromir's position in Tharbad.\n4\tBring the scattered supplies to Boromir at his position in Tharbad to the east\tBoromir is to the east, in Tharbad, taking stock of the situation and planning his next steps.\n5\tReturn to Meneldir and Egfrith on the northern bank of the Gwathló\tBoromir has agreed to return with you to meet your companions while he decides his next course.\n6\tTalk to Meneldir on the northern bank of the Gwathló\tMeneldir stares at Boromir with suspicion, his eyes narrowed.\n",
[2038]="70041323\n1\tFind crew of the Súlrohir and tell them to return to the ship (total: 5)\tThe crew of the Súlrohir are making as much merriment as they can in the Harper's Court on the west side of the city of Dol Amroth. Captain Cirnaith, fearing embarrassment, wants you to recall his crew to the Súlrohir.\n2\tReturn to the Súlrohir and study the situation\tYou have sent the crew of the Súlrohir back to their ship, and should now return to the wharf on the eastern side of Dol Amroth and see if the situation has changed. There has been a commotion on the jetty that points north-east into the water. You should investigate and learn what has happened.\n3\tTalk to Umer, the Emissary of Umbar\tUmer, an emissary of Umbar, has passed through the Sea-gate under a flag of peace. He wishes to speak with you on the docks on the eastern side of Dol Amroth.\n4\tTalk to Lothíriel in the Great Hall\tLothíriel is in the Great Hall of Dol Amroth. You have a message for Lothíriel from an emissary of Umbar, asking her to treat with his master on the deck of the flagship Night-jewel.\n",
[2039]="70061C05\n1\tTalk to Boromir and hear the tale of his journey\tMeneldir has asked the Captain of Gondor to tell the tale of his journey north, and Boromir seems willing enough to relate it.\n2\tTalk to Boromir on the northern bank of the Gwathló\tBoromir rests on the northern bank of the Gwathló, conveying the tale of his journey to you and your companions.\n",
[2040]="70041326\n1\tTalk to Lothíriel and help her decide what to do about Balakhôr's proposal\tLothíriel needs your help to decide what should be done. Lothíriel is in the Great Hall of Dol Amroth, considering Balakhôr's proposal.\n2\tTalk to Noreth on the docks\tYou were cast from the deck of the Night-jewel, and have managed to struggle back to the dock. Captain Noreth has fished you from the water, and wants to hear what happened on the Night-jewel.\n3\tTalk to Lothíriel in the Great Hall of Dol Amroth\tLothíriel is in the Great Hall of Dol Amroth. Balakhôr the Scourge has boasted of his plan to you, and now that you know his course you should bring word of it to Lothíriel.\n4\tTravel to the town of Ethring, in the Ringló Vale\tThe town of Ethring is in the Ringló Vale, on the road to Pelargir. Lothíriel has asked you to travel through the Ringló Vale and Dor-en-Ernil to help the folk of those lands and bring warning to the people of Pelargir.\n5\tTalk to Tologlor in Ethring\tTologlor in the town of Ethring has tried to catch your eye. His expression is one of frightened concern.\n",
[2041]="70000708\n1\tDefeat War-master Uzorr\030Acquire War-master Uzorr's orders\tWar-master Uzorr can be found in Bleakrift, north-west of Candaith's camp at the foot of Weathertop. Candaith asked you to find and slay War-master Uzorr and search the camp for a letter containing his orders.\n2\tBring Orc-letter to Candaith\tCandaith is at his camp at the foot of Weathertop, among the Weather Hills. You were victorious over War-master Uzorr and have obtained a letter that surely contains his orders from whatever power commands the Orcs that have ventured into the Lone-lands.\n",
[2042]="70000689\n1\tSearch the summit of Weathertop for anything unusual\tWeathertop towers above Candaith's camp. Candaith asked you to search Weathertop for anything out of the ordinary and to bring any news or evidence that you may find back to him.\n2\tBring the rock-rubbing to Candaith\tCandaith's camp is at the foot of Weathertop. You found a rune-covered rock and took a rubbing of the markings. You should return to Candaith and learn if he knows what the runes might mean.\n",
[2043]="70041325\n1\tDefeat Orcs in the Ringló Vale (total: 8)\030Collect suitable tinder (total: 4)\tOrcs can be found to the north-east of Ethring, in the Ringló Vale. Suitable tinder can also be found to the north-east. Tologlor has asked you to defeat Orcs made bold by the continuing night that blankets the Ringló Vale, and to gather suitable tinder to light the town's torches.\n2\tBring suitable tinder to Tologlor at the entrance to Ethring\tTologlor is at the entrance of the town of Ethring, waiting for you to return with news of your successes against the Orcs. He also awaits delivery of any suitable tinder you have found.\n3\tStanding torches can be found throughout Ethring. You should relight any of them that have gone out.\t\n4\tTalk to Tologlor at the entrance to Ethring\tTologlor is at the entrance to the town of Ethring, in the Ringló Vale. You have lit some of the torches throughout Ethring, trying to drive back the darkness that overpowers the Vale and its people.\n",
[2044]="70061C14\n1\tTalk to Meneldir\tBoromir, his tale completed, studies the faces of your companions. Meneldir stares back impassively.\n2\tJoin Meneldir a short distance away from the others, to the north-east\tMeneldir has asked to speak with you some distance from the others, just to the north-east of the camp-site.\n3\tTalk to Meneldir to the north-east, away from your other companions\tMeneldir wishes to speak with you about his concerns about Boromir, the Captain of Gondor.\n4\tShow the map to Boromir at the camp-site\tBoromir remains at the camp-fire near the northern bank of the Gwathló. Meneldir gave you a worn map of Old Cardolan to show to Boromir and to Egfrith.\n5\tShow the map to Egfrith at the camp-site\tEgfrith remains at the camp-fire near the northern bank of the Gwathló. Meneldir gave you a worn map of Old Cardolan to show to Boromir and to Egfrith.\n6\tTalk to Meneldir at the camp-site\tMeneldir has come back to the camp-site.\n7\tDefeat foes within Tharbad (total: 12)\030Look out over the surrounding countryside\030Find a gap in the outer wall of Tharbad to the north-west\030Find a gap in the outer wall of Tharbad further to the west\tMeneldir suggested that you scout the countryside outside Tharbad from a number of locations within the city, and defeat the foes you encounter there, to make safe your passage through the flooded city.\n8\tTalk to Meneldir on the road just north of Tharbad\tMeneldir and the others planned to meet with you on the road north of Tharbad.\n",
[2045]="70000703\n1\tTalk to Candaith and retake Weathertop with a fellowship\tCandaith is at his camp at the foot of Weathertop. The Ranger Candaith asked you to assist him in driving a company of Orcs from Weathertop. He told you to gather allies and return to him when you are prepared.\n2\tTalk to Candaith\tCandaith is at his camp at the foot of Weathertop. Candaith is waiting to discuss with you the strange events that occurred atop Amon Sûl.\n",
[2046]="7001BA6A\n1\tTalk to Candaith and retake Weathertop\tCandaith is at his camp at the foot of Weathertop. The Ranger Candaith asked you to assist him in driving a company of Orcs from Weathertop.\n2\tTalk to Candaith\tCandaith is at his camp at the foot of Weathertop. Candaith is waiting to discuss with you the strange events that occurred atop Amon Sûl.\n",
[2047]="70041327\n1\tTravel to the town of Linhir, in Dor-en-Ernil\tTologlor has asked you to check on his brother Ingalad in the town of Linhir, to the south of Ethring in Dor-en-Ernil. Tologlor is worried for his brother, who lives in the town of Linhir.\n2\tTalk to Ingalad in Linhir\tIngalad is somewhere within the town of Linhir, in Dor-en-Ernil. Tologlor of Ethring has asked you to check on his brother Ingalad in the town of Linhir.\n3\tDefeat Corsairs in Dor-en-Ernil (total: 8)\030Defeat Haradrim in Dor-en-Ernil (total: 6)\030Find Barad Rill, the lighthouse in Dor-en-Ernil, to the south-west of Linhir\tIngalad has told you of a lighthouse to the south-west, from which you might get a good view of the progress of the Corsair fleet. He also wishes for you to defeat the Corsairs and Haradrim that plague Dor-en-Ernil.\n4\tTalk to Ingalad in Linhir\tIngalad is in the town of Linhir. You have scouted the progress of the Corsair fleet and defeated many of the foes that plague Dor-en-Ernil.\n5\tSearch the Corsair camp to the north-east of Linhir for Roniel\tIngalad believes that Roniel may have fallen prey to Corsairs at a camp to the north-east, and wants you to search for the child.\n6\tCollect ragged doll from the Corsair camp\tA ragged doll in the Corsair camp north-east of Linhir has caught your attention\n7\tContinue searching north-east of the Corsair camp for Roniel\tIf Roniel did flee Linhir to the north-east, and dropped her doll as she passed the Corsair camp, she may have continued in that direction. You should continue your search to the north-east.\n8\tTalk to Roamingstar by the Gilrain\tA beautiful woman stands by the river, keeping watch on the sleeping Roniel. You should learn what you can about this woman.\n",
[2048]="70061C15\n1\tFind the south-east entrance of the town of Herne, along the road north-west of Tharbad\tHerne is located north-west of Tharbad, along the Old South Road. Meneldir told you that when he last came this way, the inn at the cross-road was a pleasant house of refreshment for travellers, and should be still.\n2\tTalk to the nearby townsman\tSomething is not right in the town of Herne. Perhaps one of the residents of the town can explain what has happened.\n3\tTalk to the nearby townsman\tSomething is not right in the town of Herne. Perhaps one of the residents of the town can explain what has happened.\n4\tTalk to the nearby townswoman\tSomething is not right in the town of Herne. Perhaps one of the residents of the town can explain what has happened.\n5\tTalk to the nearby townswoman\tSomething is not right in the town of Herne. Perhaps one of the residents of the town can explain what has happened.\n6\tEnter Crossway House, the tavern of Herne, in search of answers\tCrossway House, the inn at the cross-road, is near the southern road that passes through Herne. Something happened at Herne that has upset the townspeople. Perhaps answers await inside Crossway House, the inn at the cross-road.\n7\tTalk to Maddoc inside Crossway House\tMaddoc, the innkeeper of Crossway House, stands behind the counter.\n8\tTalk to Boromir inside Crossway House\tBoromir stands within Crossway House.\n9\tTalk to Maddoc inside Crossway House\tMaddoc, the innkeeper of Crossway House, stands behind the counter.\n10\tTalk to Meneldir inside Crossway House\tMeneldir stands inside Crossway House.\n11\tTalk to Aberthol inside his home in the northern part of Herne\tAberthol lives in the northern part of Herne. Maddoc told you something happened to Aberthol four nights ago, and the old man may speak to you about it, if you loosen his lips with a mug of his favourite spiced beer.\n12\tSet the mug of spiced beer on Aberthol's table\tA mug of spiced beer, set on his table, may encourage Aberthol to tell you what happened to him.\n13\tTalk to Aberthol inside his home\tAberthol is inside his home, considering you, your companions, and the mug of spiced beer you brought him.\n14\tIntroduce Boromir to Aberthol\030Introduce Egfrith to Aberthol\tAberthol waits for you to introduce him to your companions.\n15\tTalk to Aberthol inside his home\tAberthol, apparently awestruck by his visitors, is now willing to tell you his story.\n",
})
